AdaptiveCurveIrm::setIrmConfig(AdaptiveCurveIrmConfig)
├── given caller is not the owner
│   └── when market is unset or bound and the configuration is invalid
│       └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount before market queries or validation and preserve state
├── given caller is owner and market is unset
│   └── it should revert with IrmMarketNotSet before configuration validation and preserve state
└── given caller is owner and market is bound
    ├── when querying the market pause status fails even with an invalid configuration
    │   └── it should bubble the query revert before configuration validation and preserve all state
    ├── when active market accounting overflows after calling back even with an invalid configuration
    │   └── it should bubble arithmetic panic 0x11 and roll back both market accounting and IRM state
    ├── given the proposed configuration is invalid
    │   ├── when curveSteepness is below 1.01e18 or above 100e18
    │   │   └── it should revert with IrmInvalidParams
    │   ├── when adjustmentSpeed is below 2e18 per year or above 1000e18 per year
    │   │   └── it should revert with IrmInvalidParams
    │   ├── when targetUtilization is negative zero or above 1e18
    │   │   └── it should revert with IrmInvalidParams
    │   ├── when initialRateAtTarget is below minRateAtTarget or above maxRateAtTarget
    │   │   └── it should revert with IrmInvalidParams
    │   ├── when minRateAtTarget or maxRateAtTarget is outside 0.001e18 per year through 10e18 per year
    │   │   └── it should revert with IrmInvalidParams
    │   ├── when minRateAtTarget exceeds maxRateAtTarget
    │   │   └── it should revert with IrmInvalidParams
    │   ├── when market is paused
    │   │   └── it should leave configuration IRState and market accounting unchanged without accruing
    │   └── when market is active
    │       └── it should attempt accrual before validation then roll back all accrual and configuration effects
    └── given the proposed configuration is valid
        ├── when market is active
        │   ├── it should query the exact PAUSE_TYPE and accrue exactly once using the old configuration
        │   ├── it should add interest at the old rate to market supply and borrowed assets and update lastUpdate through the callback
        │   └── it should emit the callback IRStateUpdated then the market AccrueInterest with exact payloads before the setter events
        ├── when the active market has already adapted its rate upward and a different valid configuration is supplied
        │   ├── it should accrue only since the prior checkpoint using the adapted rate and old configuration
        │   └── it should reset to the new initialRateAtTarget after emitting the adapted-rate accrual events
        ├── when market is paused
        │   └── it should query the exact PAUSE_TYPE skip accrual and preserve lastUpdate
        ├── when curveSteepness and adjustmentSpeed are at either inclusive boundary
        │   └── it should accept and store each boundary
        ├── when targetUtilization is one wei or 1e18
        │   └── it should accept and store each boundary
        ├── when minimum initial and maximum rates are all equal at either absolute rate boundary
        │   └── it should accept and store the equal rates
        ├── when configuration is unchanged and market is active
        │   └── it should still accrue reset the rate and emit the setter events
        ├── when configuration is unchanged and the paused market has already adapted its rate
        │   └── it should reset the adapted rate to initialRateAtTarget while retaining the prior checkpoint
        ├── it should store every new configuration field and reset rateAtTarget to the new initialRateAtTarget
        ├── it should preserve owner and market
        └── it should emit IRStateUpdated then SetIrmConfig with exact payloads and no extra events
